{"text": "Timeline on Unrecognized, Single-Gender Social Organizations\nPolicy\n\nMay 6, 2016\n\nHarvard College makes initial recommendations for addressing unrecognized,\nsingle-gender social organizations (USGSOs) to President Drew Faust, she accepts.\n\nMay 22, 2016\n\nProfessor Harry Lewis and 11 other faculty members file a motion that \u201cHarvard\nCollege shall not discriminate against students on the basis of organizations they\njoin.\u201d\nSeptember 20, 2016\n\nHarvard College Dean Rakesh Khurana convenes the USGSOs Implementation\nCommittee, chaired by Professors Doug Melton and Kay Shelemay and composed of\nfaculty, students, and staff, to offer recommendations for implementing the 2016\nUSGSOs policy.\n\nJanuary 25, 2017\n\nHarvard College Dean Rakesh Khurana recommends to Faculty of Arts and Sciences\nDean Mike Smith that he establish a faculty committee to consider whether the\n2016 USGSOs policy can be improved, either by changing aspects of its existing\nstructure or through some broader revision. He has accepted that recommendation\n\nJanuary 30, 2017\nProfessor Harry Lewis and his co-signers withdraw their motion.\nFebruary 17, 2017\n\nThe Implementation Committee issues its final report with recommendations for\nimplementing the 2016 USGSOs policy.\n\nMarch 6, 2017\n\nHarvard College Dean Rakesh Khurana responds to Implementation Committee\nreport.\n\nMarch 7, 2017\n\nFaculty of Arts and Sciences Dean Mike Smith formally establishes faculty\ncommittee to gather and evaluate suggestions related to the 2016 USGSOs policy.\n\nJuly 12, 2017\nUSGSOs Faculty Committee issues preliminary recommendations.\nAugust 22, 2017",
